        "original_id": "b3df541a-6613-55e9-9c8a-126300902ade",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: Trogloxene\n- Animals: raccoons, rats, foxes, bears, opiliones, cave bears, cave lions, cave leopards, cave hyenas, Panthera leo spelaea\n\nFacts:\n- Trogloxene includes extant animals such as raccoons, rats, foxes, bears, and opiliones, also known as Daddy-Long-Legs.\n- Trogloxene also includes extinct animals such as cave bears, cave lions, cave leopards, and cave hyenas.\n- Panthera leo spelaea, also called P. spelaea, was an extinct lion subspecies commonly known as the European cave lion or Eurasian cave lion.\n- Panthera leo spelaea is known from fossils and from many examples of prehistoric art.",
